{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/639897-inspirations-for-lost","id":639897,"title":"Inspirations for Lost","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-25T23:51:22-07:00","id":639897,"title":"Inspirations for Lost","content":"Here's my Inspirations section for Second Edition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-second-edition-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-second-edition-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\"> Changeling the Lost, Second Edition Inspirations &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-second-edition-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-second-edition-inspirations/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T23:53:19-07:00","id":639919,"title":"","content":"The music link isn't working. :/<br /> <br /> I will never have enough Changeling music.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T00:49:50-07:00","id":639941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/639897-inspirations-for-lost?p=639919#post639919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The music link isn't working. :/<br /> <br /> I will never have enough Changeling music.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weird. Try this: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jlph0iL_Ivo\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jlph0iL_Ivo</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T14:42:39-07:00","id":640665,"title":"","content":"Inspiration for me is Deep Space Nine. <br /> <br /> Garak as a Darkling<br /> <br /> Jadzia Dax as a Fairest.<br /> <br /> Worf as Orge<br /> <br /> Miles O'brian and Nog as Wizen and Vic Fountan as Wizen Ministral.<br /> <br /> Benajmin Sisko as a Grimm.<br /> <br /> Odo as an Elemental.<br /> <br /> Quark as a Beast.<br /> <br /> The Wadi as Risktakers.<br /> <br /> There are even Onieromancy episodes sort of, not to mention the holosuits as a metaphor for dreams.<br /> <br /> They're is even briefly a being that plays a pact making fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 08-26-2015, 06:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T16:14:24-07:00","id":640777,"title":"","content":"I don't post often, read everything though, I desperately love Changeling. I just wanted to quickly ask about the inspirations however.<br /> <br /> Reading the list of inspirations you are drawing from for the new edition, I just wanted to ask if you are drawing on the old origins for changeling tales, at least in Europe. Oisin and Niamh, Tam Lyn, Thomas the Rhymer, and the Voyage of Brandon being the big ones. If you are pushing away from themes of mental illness with the second edition, I really would love to suggest them. Changeling has always seemed to have a strange lack of connection with Ireland and Britain in the published material, I thought this would be a good moment to see if these connections would be opened.<br /> <br /> For an example of how connected Changelings were to the region, there is reference to a man changeling testing a woman, laying her on a hot shovel, in Tipperary, just at the beginning of the twentieth century.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T17:20:59-07:00","id":640837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/639897-inspirations-for-lost?p=640777#post640777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't post often, read everything though, I desperately love Changeling. I just wanted to quickly ask about the inspirations however.<br /> <br /> Reading the list of inspirations you are drawing from for the new edition, I just wanted to ask if you are drawing on the old origins for changeling tales, at least in Europe. Oisin and Niamh, Tam Lyn, Thomas the Rhymer, and the Voyage of Brandon being the big ones. If you are pushing away from themes of mental illness with the second edition, I really would love to suggest them. Changeling has always seemed to have a strange lack of connection with Ireland and Britain in the published material, I thought this would be a good moment to see if these connections would be opened.<br /> <br /> For an example of how connected Changelings were to the region, there is reference to a man changeling testing a woman, laying her on a hot shovel, in Tipperary, just at the beginning of the twentieth century.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not pushing away from mental illness, per se. I'm just touching it with a more delicate hand. It's not &quot;madness&quot;. <br /> <br /> But yes, we've been doing a lot of fairy tale reading, from all over the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T20:13:06-07:00","id":641020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/639897-inspirations-for-lost?p=640837#post640837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not pushing away from mental illness, per se. I'm just touching it with a more delicate hand. It's not &quot;madness&quot;.<br /> <br /> But yes, we've been doing a lot of fairy tale reading, from all over the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds brilliant, I am very glad to hear it. I was always so disappointed that first edition barely touched on the real-world genesis of Changeling myths. The old core book only mentioned Thomas the Rhymer and Tam Lyn in one sentence passing. With Niamh and Oisin, and The Voyage of Bran as being the sources (as far as I know) for the altered flow of time in European Fairylands, being entirely left out as far as I can remember (though I very well could be wrong). Where other splats touched on their real-world genesis far more often, even just to debunk or restructure them into the outlook of the game line, Changeling always felt like it was avoiding it.<br /> <br /> I have also thought the social practice of 'removing' infants, children, or adults believed to be Changelings (in game terms, they would be the Fetches) in both Ireland and Wales would have been something the game could have touched on to better root itself in its real world origins. Mortals knew about Changelings and Fetches, and were actively hunting them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T03:41:57-07:00","id":641344,"title":"","content":"Now I don't like to tell you that you are missing something very important... BUT OH MY GOD YOU ARE MISSING SOMETHING VERY IMPORTANT UNDER GAMES!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7a_St9DTuO0\" target=\"_blank\">Where is the big bad wolf?!</a><br /> <br /> Seriously, this game is like... PLAY IT IF YOU LIKE CHANGELING YOU LITTLE...!<br /> <br /> Here is a synopsis for you: PLAY THE FRIKKIN GAME!<br /> <br /> Music is sweet as hell too!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_hNMZWlaPRU\" data-code=\"_hNMZWlaPRU\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/_hNMZWlaPRU/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> (Seriously, there is a talking pig in this game. Just check it.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VfOoxMha73A\" data-code=\"VfOoxMha73A\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/VfOoxMha73A/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> EDIT: It also touches an interesting aspect which I never found enough of in my changeling games... People remembering things that happened during their captivity and maybe what they did to each other. How will the beast hound feel about the kennel-master ogre that whipped and beat them every day on the orders of their keeper when the two of them are free and spending time together in a freehold?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6030,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","user":"A_Newfie","date":". 08-27-2015, 06:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T04:51:52-07:00","id":641397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A_Newfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/639897-inspirations-for-lost?p=641344#post641344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I don't like to tell you that you are missing something very important... BUT OH MY GOD YOU ARE MISSING SOMETHING VERY IMPORTANT UNDER GAMES!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7a_St9DTuO0\" target=\"_blank\">Where is the big bad wolf?!</a><br /> <br /> Seriously, this game is like... PLAY IT IF YOU LIKE CHANGELING YOU LITTLE...!<br /> <br /> Here is a synopsis for you: PLAY THE FRIKKIN GAME!<br /> <br /> Music is sweet as hell too!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_hNMZWlaPRU\" data-code=\"_hNMZWlaPRU\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/_hNMZWlaPRU/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> (Seriously, there is a talking pig in this game. Just check it.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VfOoxMha73A\" data-code=\"VfOoxMha73A\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/VfOoxMha73A/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> EDIT: It also touches an interesting aspect which I never found enough of in my changeling games... People remembering things that happened during their captivity and maybe what they did to each other. How will the beast hound feel about the kennel-master ogre that whipped and beat them every day on the orders of their keeper when the two of them are free and spending time together in a freehold?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a huge fan. Oddly, I didn't really like Fables as a comic. But Wolf Among Us was really good. I think I will add it to the list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T05:05:54-07:00","id":641401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/639897-inspirations-for-lost?p=641397#post641397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm a huge fan. Oddly, I didn't really like Fables as a comic. But Wolf Among Us was really good. I think I will add it to the list.</div> </div> </div> </div>When my grandchildren grow up, I'll tell them I had an influence on the second edition of Changeling the lost!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T09:47:41-07:00","id":644335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/639897-inspirations-for-lost?p=640777#post640777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For an example of how connected Changelings were to the region, there is reference to a man changeling testing a woman, laying her on a hot shovel, in Tipperary, just at the beginning of the twentieth century.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are actually several stories that are similar to elements of the Lost. &quot;A man from Lios P\u00f3il&quot; describes a man who is abducted by the S\u00ed/fairies and made to serve them.<br /> <br /> Eventually he escapes when they leave their fort to abduct somebody else. He attempts to wrestle the guardian goblin to leave, during the fight he accidently rubs some fairy material on one of his eyes, allowing him to see in the dark and he defeats the guard. Making his way home, he finds his own funeral occurring as the fetch left in his place has died. He does convince his family that he is the real one, but is forever left with one eye able to see the Fae as they move in our world.<br /> <br /> (Although in some versions of the story, he has his uncle punch the eye out of his head!)<br /> <br /> There are also stories of pipers are abducted and made to entertain the fairies against their will, returning later with the ability to play Fae music. Often this leaves them outcasts (they will naturally burst into the Fae music at festivals, haunting others) and they often become alcoholics to forget it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T18:26:25-07:00","id":646172,"title":"","content":"On the video game front, I think the Alan Wake games are a great source of inspiration for Changeling. It starts with a strange abduction and features long tracks of wilderness, doppelgangers with shadowy powers, and the act of trying to fight free of a narrative. Plus the Dark Presence is one of the more perfect examples I've ever seen of a Fae as described in Equinox Road.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T00:54:46-07:00","id":647762,"title":"","content":"Curious about movies like Labyrinth, granted it is obvious, but it fits so perfectly with Changeling even if it has a happy ending and is somewhat lighthearted for WoD...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T06:13:16-07:00","id":651084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madfox11</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/639897-inspirations-for-lost?p=647762#post647762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Curious about movies like Labyrinth, granted it is obvious, but it fits so perfectly with Changeling even if it has a happy ending and is somewhat lighthearted for WoD...</div> </div> </div> </div>Labyrinth and Pan's labyrinth are both wicked, even if Labyrinth is more on the lighthearted side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T18:40:27-07:00","id":653325,"title":"","content":"I'm always really inspired by the band Caravan of Thieves for Changeling (and WoD in general). The song &quot;Sister Went Missing&quot; from <a href=\"https://play.spotify.com/user/11150486461/playlist/4XRA6i7uqZZNhhD6PrXFbb?play=true&amp;utm_source=open.spotify.com&amp;utm_medium=open\" target=\"_blank\">Funhouse</a> sounds exactly like a Fae abduction and escape, but from the point of view of those left behind. A Gentry comes to town, heralded by bells and balloons, and no one can stop It taking one little girl. The girl's family tries to get her back, blaming the odd Mr. Hill, and taking their bloody revenge on him. Which is all fine, until the girl comes home...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T00:54:40-07:00","id":653623,"title":"","content":"On the anime/music front, I recommend the original <b>.hack//sign</b> anime (<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eimOB2r6kuw\" target=\"_blank\"><u>trailer</u></a>), along with Yuki Kaijura's soundtrack for the show. Its set in an immersive VR massive multiplayer online RPG, but plays with many of the same themes as <i>Lost</i>. Running from an abusive life, the player Tsukasa turned to fantasy as a temporary escape. Then <i>SHE</i> spoke, and a pact was struck. And now Tsukasa can no longer feel his VR wraps, or log out. The game world is now his home . . . whether he wants to stay or not. . .<br /> <br /> The anime itself was crippled by an extensive focus on the &quot;normal&quot; players - but that could work for a <i>Changeling</i> campaign, particularly if you want ideas for what it would be like for &quot;normal&quot; humans at risk of getting dragged into the affairs of changelings.<br /> <br /> As for the soundtrack - I don't think there's an official video or authorized uploads online. But if you search for them, they're there, and work really. Yuki Kaijura used Latin and Spanish music, slowed <i>way</i> down, to create very haunting vocals. In particular, look for &quot;In the Land of Twilight, Underneath the Moon&quot;, &quot;Key of Twilight&quot;, and &quot;Aura&quot;.<br /> <br /> In a radically different direction - If you're looking at a crossover with the God-Machine (or maybe <i>Promethean</i>), I highly recommend Orgy's <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NczLNctogZk\" target=\"_blank\"><u>Fiction (Dreams in Digital)</u></a>. Or, for more of a gritty/street game, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=o1tj2zJ2Wvg\" target=\"_blank\"><u>Welcome to the Jungle</u></a> (by Guns'n'Roses) is a good choice..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madfox11</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/639897-inspirations-for-lost?p=647762#post647762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Curious about movies like Labyrinth, granted it is obvious, but it fits so perfectly with Changeling even if it has a happy ending and is somewhat lighthearted for WoD...</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Labyrinth</b> (<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XRcOZZDvMv4\" target=\"_blank\"><u>trailer</u></a>) works well for both <i>Changeling</i> games (both <i>Lost</i> and <i>Dreaming</i>), as does <b>Coraline </b>(<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LO3n67BQvh0\" target=\"_blank\"><u>trailer</u></a>). The otherwise forgettable <b>Mirrormask</b> (<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=swrcKRVgeGI\" target=\"_blank\"><u>trailer</u></a>) has a great scene for <i>Lost</i>, where the girl finds a way to spy on her Fetch, and starts yelling at her to stop kissing a particular boy, because &quot;he's horrible&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":".  added trailers 09-06-2015, 04:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T17:52:34-07:00","id":665103,"title":"","content":"The song from the recent Endless Legend trailer seems like it fits Changeling quite well:<br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=07YPiD4UZr4\" target=\"_blank\"><u><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=07YPiD4UZr4\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=07YPiD4UZr4</a></u></a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>\u201cThe good sleep better, but the bad seem to enjoy the waking hours much more.\u201d</b> -<i>Woody Allen</i> \u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5322-zimthehacker","name":"Zimthehacker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5322_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T01:44:33-07:00","id":666619,"title":"","content":"Friend of mine recommended me a <i><b>Natsume's Book of Friends</b></i> ( jap. <a href=\"http://shinden.pl/anime/6600-natsume-yuujinchou\" target=\"_blank\">Natsume Yuujinchou</a> ) anime about boy called Takeshi that all his life see <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Yokai</span></span></span> ( the Japan's fae ), that get his &quot;gift&quot; after grandmother - so he is probably Fea-Touched. He get his grandmother &quot;Book of Friends&quot; in that she sealed a Yokai names with the Pledges ( or maybe Contracts ) after winning with them in fight. ( Maybe she was Summer Courtier? ) Now Yokai want Takeshi to free them from their Pledge or want to steal &quot;Book of Friends&quot; to command other Yokai. Takeshi is helped by the wolf &quot;demon&quot; Madara locked in the body of &quot;fortune cat&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Great series as inspiration for Japanese <b>Changeling</b>, hope it's parts will be used at least in Tokyo setting. Here is trailer:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mea4xITAo_4\" data-code=\"mea4xITAo_4\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/mea4xITAo_4/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T10:30:46-07:00","id":681091,"title":"","content":"As yesterday started next season, I point you to...<br /> <br /> <i><b>Once Upon a Time</b></i><br /> <br /> Epic story of characters from fairy tales that come to human world and try to make their both halves fairy and mundane life work together - by founding their new identity after them. The series revolves on themes of good and bad ( or Virtue and Vice in WoD terms ), heroes and villains, and in the end how the lines separating them are very thin. Almost all of characters would be of Fairest or Grimm 2ED Seemings - because even the &quot;wicked&quot; are &quot;most perfect of the all&quot;. It's really a superb modern fairy tale and great source for <b>Changeling</b>'s ideas. And you can - literally - be ripped of your heart!<br /> <br /> Just see a fan trailer below. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gMJiMvqELEA\" data-code=\"gMJiMvqELEA\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/gMJiMvqELEA/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-28-2015, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T02:02:50-07:00","id":686703,"title":"","content":"Some non-American films and sources of inspiration<br /> <br /> Tale of Tales (Italian-British-French 2015) <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=J9ETi804w-E\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=J9ETi804w-E</a><br /> <br /> El Belle et la Bette (French 2014, The Beauty and the Beast with a twist, full movie, fabulous aesthetically) <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oKA9R1Nn_yI\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oKA9R1Nn_yI</a><br /> <br /> Viy (Russian film 2014, based loosely on Gogol's short story) <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CPcPtizGymc\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CPcPtizGymc</a> <br /> <br /> = Viy was also released as &quot;Forbidden Empire&quot; (for some unknown reason) in full English <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Cj0keIGgJNE\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Cj0keIGgJNE</a> <br /> <br /> Night Watch (Russian film 2006, based on Fyodor Lukanyenko's book series also available on Amazon in English) <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yMHQsjgQDrA\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yMHQsjgQDrA</a><br /> <br /> Day Watch (Russian film 2007, part 2 from above) <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S8VDpuJEQGw\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S8VDpuJEQGw</a><br /> <br /> <br /> Animated Music Videos:from Theodor Bastard (dark trip-hop &amp; neofolk band from St Petersburg):<br /> <br /> Selva (inspired by Russian folktales) <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iMDp6vtaqKU\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iMDp6vtaqKU</a><br /> <br /> Pustota (Emptiness)<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qb_-hMsaD9g\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qb_-hMsaD9g\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qb_-hMsaD9g\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qb_-hMsaD9g </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This is where I set my Changeling the Lost chronicle (and actually live next to) - The Tsaritsyno Palace &amp; Estate Parks in Moscow, Russia:<br /> I try to combine Russian/Slavic, Norse, Tatar, and Scythian/Kipchak folklore and mythology rather than more standard Celtic)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tsaritsyno_Park\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9b/Tsaritsino_from_helicopter-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tsaritsyno_Park\" target=\"_blank\"> Tsaritsyno Palace - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tsaritsyno_Park\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tsaritsyno_Park </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> pics<br /> <a href=\"https://www.google.ru/search?q=tsaritsyno+park&amp;newwindow=1&amp;espv=2&amp;biw=1920&amp;bih=979&amp;tbm=isch&amp;tbo=u&amp;source=univ&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=0CDcQsARqFQoTCL3ElY31pcgCFcKEcgodUokDKw\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.google.ru/search?q=tsari...FcKEcgodUokDKw</a><br /> <br /> map <a href=\"http://forum.nanya.ru/uploads/post-14149-1157208484.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.nanya.ru/uploads/post-14149-1157208484.jpg</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8207-the-scythian","user":"The Scythian","date":". 10-03-2015, 07:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8207-the-scythian","name":"The Scythian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8207_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T03:45:23-07:00","id":688069,"title":"","content":"I think that maybe &quot;Tale of Tales&quot; doesn't feat very well (maybe just one tale, the one with Ogre in it) it is far from setting and atmosphere of changeling.<br /> <br /> Two song that maybe may be inside the Changeling mood:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LS-DB-oUMgI\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LS-DB-oUMgI\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LS-DB-oUMgI\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LS-DB-oUMgI </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> and, of course, this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=R3WwcsjWPIQ\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=R3WwcsjWPIQ\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=R3WwcsjWPIQ\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=R3WwcsjWPIQ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7277-brighella","name":"Brighella","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T07:46:51-07:00","id":688322,"title":"","content":"Some things that inspired me for Changeling the Lost games:<br /> -Revolutionary Girl Utena: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6FX5iMvJx-0\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6FX5iMvJx-0</a> The Academy is a cool Fae Realm, and Akio a creepy Keeper.<br /> -The City of Lost Children: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Pa7oVPru4J8\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Pa7oVPru4J8</a> Dream stealing, abductions...<br /> -Code Lyoko: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Cu1TM2ZxhTM\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Cu1TM2ZxhTM</a> Lyoko could be the Hedge, with bunch of Changelings protecting it and the mortal world from the True Fae Xana.<br /> -Now and Then, Here and There: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BsYY0ReMGz0\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BsYY0ReMGz0</a> for being displaced in a horrifying world, and examples of literally every kind of abuse, trauma and horror one could imagine.<br /> -Soul Eater: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=D-WXvtPtfRY\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=D-WXvtPtfRY</a> mostly for the focus on insanity.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T09:34:21-07:00","id":689800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/639897-inspirations-for-lost?p=653623#post653623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Coraline </b>(<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LO3n67BQvh0\" target=\"_blank\"><u>trailer</u></a>).</div> </div> </div> </div>Echoing this recommendation. Coraline is one of my all-time favorite Changeling-esque movies. Seriously, it's about a lonely little girl who's seduced into visiting a fantastical yet creepy otherworld, and eventually has to rescue her parents from it when it intrudes too deeply into their lives. The Other Mother is perfect inspiration for a True Fae.<br /> <br /> And if that's not enough, it's by Neil Gaiman!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T09:39:35-07:00","id":689828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/639897-inspirations-for-lost?p=688322#post688322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some things that inspired me for Changeling the Lost games:<br /> -Revolutionary Girl Utena: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6FX5iMvJx-0\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6FX5iMvJx-0</a> The Academy is a cool Fae Realm, and Akio a creepy Keeper.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Always and forever, Utena. Had I a say on the matter, it would be listed in the corebook.<br /> <br /> Also, anyone mention <a href=\"http://tale-of-tales.com/ThePath/\" target=\"_blank\">The Path</a>? Because The Path is another one I would put in the core book. Certainly I'm going to be pulling from it for The Hedge.<br /> <br /> And while we're at it, Majora's Mask. Because dear god, is that game swimming in the themes of Changeling.<br /> <br /> And Alan Wake, for being a Changeling story wrapped up in urban legends, ghost stories, and weird pulp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-05-2015, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T19:37:16-07:00","id":1139334,"title":"","content":"I suggest a couple of webcomics:<br /> White Noise at white-noise-comic.com is about changeling fugitives fleeing from genocide and slavers to a land of spirits where they are not wanted.<br /> <br /> Artificial Incident at ai.katbox.net is about a young man playing a female dark elf in a MMORPG. After about a year of play he/she experiences excruciating pain and wakes up inside what was once the game world. 300 years have passed since the adventurers vanished and new stars appeared in the sky. The character has all her in game skills and items and remembers the back story she gave herself as real memories, but her previous life as a man is fading from her memories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T22:05:33-08:00","id":1192967,"title":"","content":"Itching to run a Christmas themed Changeling chronicle centered around The Nutcracker. Holiday horror, great fun! Perhaps next winter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23821,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23821-rathford","user":"Rathford","date":". 03-08-2018, 01:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23821-rathford","name":"Rathford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23821_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T23:49:54-08:00","id":1192990,"title":"","content":"Annihilation.<br /> <br /> Mostly in that the Shimmer being good visual inspiration for the Hedge and Arcadia: beautiful and ethereal yet also terrifying and dangerous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T13:52:53-08:00","id":1193298,"title":"","content":"Princess tutu for the story of some Grimm changlings and ancient Magnus bride for fae creatures","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T20:08:03-08:00","id":1193789,"title":"","content":"This song by Tom Waits is a big inspiration for a character I am writing. It brings a tear to my eye whenever I hear it.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S-7vMQyr_LI\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S-7vMQyr_LI\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S-7vMQyr_LI\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S-7vMQyr_LI </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10343-the-anubi","name":"The Anubi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T15:36:11-07:00","id":1195870,"title":"","content":"I think Little Nightmares fits in perfectly with Lost.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VCn430sHLxs\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VCn430sHLxs\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VCn430sHLxs\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VCn430sHLxs </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T02:31:10-07:00","id":1197528,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://youtu.be/73wmh4eiRR4\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/73wmh4eiRR4</a> What is this","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T18:34:19-07:00","id":1244007,"title":"","content":"As above so below, as below so above. The macrocosm is in the microcosm and the microcosm is in the macrocosm. Borrowing from yesterday's newspaper: the Russian investigation is still ongoing in Washington, and the Scottish rite Freemasons are selling two properties because declining membership means they can't keep them up. <br /> <br /> As above so below, as below so above, every country on Earth has a corresponding nation/territory in Arcadia, I will call the Fae nation corresponding to Russia Muscovy. As Russian influence spreads here in drear mundania: that's a Xanth reference, Muscovy influence spreads in Arcadia.<br /> <br /> Masonic mystery plays helped strengthen the Fae realm corresponding to the United States, their declining numbers have weakened that Fae realm. I will call the Fae realm for the United States Galunlati from the book Darkthunder's Way by Tom Deitz. I think he got it from James Mooney's Myths of the Cherokee.<br /> <br /> I see in TV listings that an upcoming episode of Ancient Aliens is titled Russia Declassified. Baba Yaga and Koschi the Deathless are posing as aliens and feeding information to the Russian government.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T00:35:10-07:00","id":1244070,"title":"","content":"&quot;Quicksand House&quot; by Carlton Mellick III<br /> <br /> It's as if Franz Kafka tried to write children's fantasy. Most of the book is an incredible example of a Durance and a later escape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T18:03:38-07:00","id":1244335,"title":"","content":"I remember a quote from a kickstarter video for a book of new fairy tales. Wish I remembered the title. I don't, but I did remember part of the intro vid. I found that quote inspiring.<br /> <br /> &quot;Children do not need fairy tales to teach them that there are monsters. Children have always known there are things hiding in the dark. What fairy tales teach...is that sometimes, if a soul is brave and clever and quick, the monsters can be fought or transformed..&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T01:23:28-07:00","id":1299540,"title":"","content":"Some of the stuff I occasionally think about are Paprika, Close Encounters, and the Doctor Who episodes &quot;Heaven Sent&quot; and &quot;It Takes You Away&quot;. &quot;Heaven Sent&quot; is a good and terrifying metaphor about grief, it has the main character trapped in a otherwordly plane, and contains a triumphant but painful escape through sheer determination. &quot;It Takes You Away&quot; contains, through fairy tale tropes, travel between dimensions complete with an Hedge, more about grief, and contact with an inmense, uncomprehensible being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25136-kev\u00e4\u00e4n-neito","user":"Kev\u00e4\u00e4n Neito","date":". 03-25-2019, 04:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25136-kev\u00e4\u00e4n-neito","name":"Kev\u00e4\u00e4n Neito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T20:17:08-07:00","id":1299828,"title":"","content":"There are worse guides than Jordan Peele's <i>Us </i>as to how terrifying, and yet sympathetic, changelings looking to murder and replace their fetches are.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Red's pretty much a changeling herself.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T08:35:12-07:00","id":1301318,"title":"","content":"This video is basically Changeling: The Music Video:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6Oh9iWDBsmE\" data-code=\"6Oh9iWDBsmE\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/6Oh9iWDBsmE/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Link if the player doesn't work: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6Oh9iWDBsmE\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6Oh9iWDBsmE</a><br /> <br /> <br /> It starts with a girl walking through a forest into a strange and eerie place with a mirror (the portal to the Hedge?). Then she's assaulted by three crones, wicked, alien, yet beautiful, who glee at her arrival (could they be True Fae?). Then they start transforming her, turning her into one of them (turning her into a changeling?). After her transformation the girl manages to find an opening to escape, and runs away, through the forest, into a lake. In the lake, underwater, the girl becomes herself again, for the most part at least, and when she comes back up, she seems like she's waking up from a dream, but she seems changed by what she saw (did she make it back through the Hedge to Earth?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 03-31-2019, 11:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T20:39:08-07:00","id":1303876,"title":"","content":"Anybody else think Happy Tree Friends would make for a good inspiration?<br /> <br /> Every day starts out looking bright and cheerful, like everything's going to turn out all right for you.<br /> <br /> But as the day wears on, things become progressively worse for you and your friends.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, the day culminates with you all being killed in horrifically gruesome accidents that seem like they belong in the Final Destination series.<br /> <br /> And then suddenly, you're revived, with all injuries miraculously healed, and the memories of your previous death having been erased.<br /> <br /> And as you awaken, the sun greets you as you prepare to set out on another beautiful day on the town!<br /> <br /> Your age and occupation in society is also inconsistent, and can fluctuate between being a grade school student, to being an adult with a full time job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T18:31:28-07:00","id":1305870,"title":"","content":"One of the books I'm reading is &quot;Tribe of Witches&quot;. The author mentions an octagon shaped nemeton dedicated to the hunting god. This reminded me of the octagon house I saw mentioned in &quot;Weird Virginia&quot;. I then thought of Saint Hubert the patron saint of hunters and foresters, so I thought the octagon house would be a good place to put a chapel of Saint Hubert. One of the other books I'm reading is Malory's Works, when the knights aren't busy smiting each other they seem to spend a lot of time visiting chapels.<br /> <br /> One of the other chapters in &quot;Tribe of Witches&quot; is about sacred trees and pillars. It seems the romans replaced some of the sacred trees in carved stone pillars. These were latter replaced with large stone crosses. The author also mentions that Nenius wrote of a mysterious ash tree that bore apples. The editorial page in my local paper has had several columns about the Bladensburg &quot;Peace Cross&quot;. I figured if you can go from sacred tree to cross, you can go from cross to sacred tree. <br /> <br /> If you don't mind PDF's there is the game Grimm by Fantasy Flight Games. I suppose in Chronicles of Darkness terms Grimm is an Innocents trapped in Arcadia setting, with Arcadia being ruled by Humpty Dumpty as the Cracked King. This reminds me of the Humphry Dumpler episodes of Beware the Batman. As I recall Humphry Dumpler wanted revenge for the loss of his family. I've never played any of the Batman or Arkham video games so I don't know if Humphry Dumpler is in them, but a large man wanting revenge for the loss of his family sounds like the Kingpin from several of the Spiderman Cartoon series.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T15:19:01-07:00","id":1339934,"title":"","content":"While I am not a CtL player, I came across a strange and clever BBC radio drama that often seems to capture the &quot;wange and stronderful.&quot; The show is called &quot;Alice's Wunderland&quot; and all episodes are currently available for free on the BBC app. Not all of it will be useful, and some of it is NSFW, but parts of it are funny-eerie-disturbing. <br /> <br /> The narrator has a grandmotherly patter of malapropisms that starts each episode: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Good eventide dear bandits! It's dead-fingery cold and the sky's full of morgue juice. I see yer back... and yer front. You are about to enter the mind-sieve of Alice's Wunderland... </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T16:45:01-07:00","id":1339957,"title":"","content":"Lo, for it has risen from its grave!<br /> <br /> Anyway, just about anything by Cosmo Sheldrake is my go-to Hedge and Arcadia background music. Just the melodies alone","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T19:52:30-07:00","id":1341042,"title":"","content":"<b>The Hole in the Ground<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/BxY2vnJiByw\" data-code=\"BxY2vnJiByw\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/BxY2vnJiByw/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}